ain strong.\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Asset: Brand is the core asset. Proxy: retail premium + franchise fee premium \u2014 evidenced by 811-hotel pipeline and retail growth 63% YoY. Not separately valued in DCF (embedded in cash flows).\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC:\n- Adjusted NOPAT FY2025 \u2248 OI $330M \u00d7 (1-25%) + R&D add-back \u2248 $270M [Estimate]\n- Adjusted invested capital = equity $514M + debt 0 + leases $182M - cash/ST inv $841M - cap R&D \u2248 -$145M (negative IC \u2014 cash-rich)\n- Adjusted ROIC is deeper than GAAP ROE (~53%); capital-light model creates negative invested capital base. GAAP vs adjusted gap > 5pts \u2014 direction favorable.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (FY2025): NI $232M + D&A $8M - maintenance capex ~$5M - \u0394WC (+$124M \u2014 source of cash) - SBC $19M \u2248 $340M [Estimate \u2014 WC swing is volatile; exclude from steady-state]. Core owner earnings \u2248 $216M after SBC.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3-1. Forecast (explicit 5-year) \u2014 ALL DRIVERS SOURCED\n\n| Year | Revenue ($B) | Growth | OP Margin | NOPAT ($B) | D&A ($B) | Capex ($B) | FCF ($B) |\n|------|--------------|--------|-----------|------------|----------|-----------|----------|\n| 2025A | 1.400 | \u2014 | 23.6% | \u2014 | 0.008 | 0.012 | 0.273 |\n| 2026E | 1.820 | +30% | 22.0% | 0.300 | 0.018 | 0.027 | 0.291 |\n| 2027E | 2.148 | +18% | 22.5% | 0.363 | 0.021 | 0.043 | 0.341 |\n| 2028E | 2.470 | +15% | 23.0% | 0.426 | 0.025 | 0.049 | 0.402 |\n| 2029E | 2.766 | +12% | 23.5% | 0.488 | 0.028 | 0.055 | 0.461 |\n| 2030E | 3.043 | +10% | 24.0% | 0.548 | 0.030 | 0.061 | 0.517 |\n\nSources for every driver:\n- 2025A revenue, OP margin, D&A, capex, FCF: Pack SECTION 5 [Actual]\n- 2026 +30%: Company FY2026 revenue guidance +24\u201328% [Actual \u2014 IR release Q1 2026]; Q2 actual +41.4% [Actual \u2014 SEC ex-99.1]; H1 +44%; consensus FY2026 +31.3% (S&P Global via stockanalysis.com) [Estimate]. Using +30% = upper end of guidance, below consensus.\n- 2027 +18%: Consensus revenue growth +18.2% (S&P Global) [Estimate]\n- 2028 +15%, 2029 +12%, 2030 +10%: [Assumption] \u2014 NOT covered by guidance or retrieved consensus. Basis: base rate for scaled China franchise platforms (Huazhu deceleration history), retail normalization from +63% to ~20\u201325%, pipeline visibility ~2 years, RevPAR near flat. This path implies 2025\u20132030 revenue CAGR ~16.8%.\n- OP margin: FY2025 23.6% [Actual]; Q2 2026 actual margin 20.9% [Arithmetic from SEC filing]; management flags slight net margin decline for 2026 on investment [Actual \u2014 earnings call excerpt, Pack \u00a710 and web brief]. 2026 22.0%, 2027 22.5%, 2028 23.0%, 2029 23.5%, 2030 24.0% \u2014 [Assumption]\n- Tax rate: 25% [Assumption] \u2014 China standard rate; GAAP effective ~30% in FY2025 [Arithmetic], but pack notes domestic-only consistency caveat.\n- D&A: ~1.0% of revenue (vs 0.6% FY2025) [Assumption]\n- Capex: 1.5% of revenue in 2026 rising to 2.0% (vs 0.9% FY2025) [Assumption] \u2014 reflects retail supply chain and tech investments flagged by management.\n- \u0394Working capital: modeled as 0 [$0.00 impact] \u2014 FY2025 showed a +$124M cash source; modeling 0 is conservative (no repeat tailwind