2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 2.5-1. R&D capitalization: ATAT is a hotel franchise/retail\ncompany; R&D is not a material financial-statement line item in the\npack. Retail product development is expensed in SG&A. Adjust beyond\nGAAP: N/A \u2014 immaterial [Assumption].\nStep 2.5-2. SBC treatment:\n\u2022 FY25 reported FCF = $0.273B [Arithmetic]; less SBC $0.019B =\n  adjusted FCF $0.254B [Arithmetic]. SBC = 1.4% of revenue \u2014 modest.\n  My primary DCF embeds SBC as an expense already within operating\n  income.\nStep 2.5-3. Operating lease capitalization:\n\u2022 Operating leases $0.182B [Actual \u2014 FY25 balance sheet]. Total debt\n  per vendor = $0.218B [Estimate] which reconciles EXACTLY as\n  $0.182B leases + $0.036B short-term debt (current portion overlaps)\n  [Arithmetic]. Therefore:\n  Net debt = -($0.475B cash + $0.366B ST investments - $0.218B debt)\n           = -$0.623B (NET CASH) [Estimate]\n  Note: company reports net cash of RMB 3.7B as of June 30, 2026\n  [Actual \u2014 Q2 2026 call] \u2248 $0.55B at 6.73 \u2014 consistent.\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/data asset estimate: 120M members [Actual], 12M\npillows sold [Actual]; brand value not independently estimated\n[Unconfirmed \u2014 not attempted].\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC: GAAP ROE 52.9%, ROIC >50% [Estimate];\nlease-adjusted invested capital would lower this by a few points\nonly \u2014 gap >5% not material.\nStep 2.5-6. Owner earnings (Buffett):\nNI $0.232B + D&A $0.008B - maintenance capex $0.005B [Assumption \u2014\nmost of $0.012B is maintenance] - \u0394 operating working capital\n($0.05B source, see below) \u2248 $0.285B [Estimate]. Very strong.\nIMPORTANT: The pack's \"change in working capital\" column (+$0.124B\nFY25) is NOT the operating \u0394WC \u2014 it includes cash and short-term\ninvestments, which moved primarily between balance-sheet categories.\nOperating working capital (receivables + inventory less non-debt\ncurrent liabilities) is deep NEGATIVE, i.e., the business runs on\nfloat; in FY25 operating \u0394WC was a modest cash SOURCE [Estimate].\nThe DCF below assumes operating \u0394WC \u2248 0 (neutral), a conservative\ntreatment.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDiscount-rate derivation [Assumption-driven, fully disclosed]:\n\u2022 Risk-free: US 10Y 4.74% [Actual] (USD-reported earnings)\n\u2022 ERP: 5.5% (US 5.0% + China-risk premium 0.5%) [Assumption]\n\u2022 Beta: 1.1 (asset-light but consumer-cyclical; vendor beta 0.65\n  rejected as too low for a China single-market name) [Assumption]\n\u2022 Cost of equity = 4.74% + 1.1 \u00d7 5.5% = 10.8% [Assumption]\n\u2022 WACC \u2248 10.0% (blend with net-cash, which earns below cost) [Assumption]\nSensitivity range tested: 9-11%.\n\nForecast drivers \u2014 ALL sourced:\n\u2022 FY2026 revenue: +30% [Actual \u2014 management guidance raised at Q2 2026]\n  \u2192 $1.820B at FY25 $1.400B \u00d7 1.30.\n\u2022 FY27-30 growth path: +22%, +16%, +12%, +9% [Assumption]. NOT\n  guided\u2014management only guides FY26. Rationale: 811 pipeline (2-3 yr\n  conversion) supports high-teens 2027; retail rises from +63% Q2 to\n  guided +40% FY26 [Actual], then decelerates toward +20% \u2192 15%;\n  hotel growth matures. The sensitivity matrix in Section 4 handles\n  the plausible range explicitly.\n\u2022 Operating margin: FY26 22.5% [Assumption \u2014 Q2 call: \"modest\n  year-over-year decline in full-year net profit margin\" due to\n  lower-margin retail/supply chain mix]; then 23.0%, 23.5%, 24.0%,\n  24.0% [Assumption \u2014 operating leverage on the fee business vs\n  retained retail dilution].\n\u2022 Tax rate: 29% FY26, 28% thereafter [Assumption \u2014 FY25 implied ~31%;\n  management cited a higher tax rate in FY26; statutory 25% + minor\n  adjustments].\n\u2022 Capex: 1.2% of revenue (rising from 0.9% due to retail and\n  technology) [Assumption].\n\u2022 D&A: 0.5% of revenue (2/3 of capex; leases are operating) [Assumption].\n\u2022 Operating \u0394WC: 0 (business runs negative-WC float) [Assumption].\n\u2022 SBC: already in op income; net share dilution offset by buyback\n  program [Assumption] \u2014 share count held at 137.5M.\n\nEXPLICIT FORECAST (USD billions; years are fiscal):\n  FY      Rev      Growth  OpInc   Tax    NOPAT   D&A   Capex   FCF\n  2025A  $1.400   +41.0%  $0.330  31%   $0.228  0.008  0.012  $0.224\n  2026E  $1.820   +30.0%  $0.409  29%   $0.290  0.009  0.022  $0.277\n  2027E  $2.220   +22.0%  $0.511  28%   $0.368  0.011  0.027  $0.352\n  2028E  $2.576   +16.0%  $0.605  28%   $0.436  0.013  0.031  $0.418\n  2029E  $2.885   +12.0%  $0.692  28%   $0.498  0.014  0.035  $0.478\n  2030E  $3.145   +9.0%   $0.755  28%   $0.544  0.016  0.038  $0.522\n\nTerminal: g = 3.5% [Assumption \u2014 China nominal GDP ~4-5% long-term\n[Assumption], discounted for platform maturity; max 4% tested].\nTerminal value = $0.522 \u00d7 1.035 / (0.10 - 0.035) = $8.31B [Arithmetic].\n\nPV @ 10%:\n  PV(FCF 2026-30) = 0.252 + 0.291 + 0.314 + 0.327 + 0.324 = $1.51B\n  PV(TV) = $8.31 / 1.611 = $5.16B\n  EV = $6.67B\n  + Net cash $0.623B (leases + ST debt as debt) \u2192 EQUITY = $7.29B\n  \u00f7 137.5M ADS \u2192 IV = $53.0/ADS [Estimate]\n\nSensitivity: IV per ADS ($):\n  WACC \\ g     2.5%    3.0%    3.5%    4.0%\n  9%           $55     $58     $62     $67\n  10%          $47     $50     $53     $56\n  11%          $41     $44     $46     $49\nBase = $53. Tornado (Top-3 drivers):\n  1. Terminal growth (g 3.0 vs 4.0 at WACC 10): -$3 / +$3 \u2192 narrowest\n  2. Operating margin FY30 (20% vs 24%): IV $44 vs $53 \u2192 \u00b1$9\n  3. Revenue CAGR (bear -15%/yr vs bull +20%/yr): $30 vs $66 \u2192 \u00b1$23\nThesis KPIs are therefore REVENUE GROWTH, MARGIN, and (embedded) WACC/\nChina-risk \u2014 in that order.\n\nMultiples cross-check [Estimate]:\n\u2022 FY26E EPS \u2248 $2.22 (NOPAT $0.290 + interest income $0.015, /137.5M)\n  \u2192 at $34.75, fwd P/E = 15.7\u00d7; at $53, 23.9\u00d7\n\u2022 FY26E EBITDA \u2248 $0.418B \u2192 EV/EBITDA at $34.75 = 9.9\u00d7; at $53 = 16.0\u00d7\n\u2022 Peer HTHT (Huazhu): market cap $15.1B, trailing P/E ~35\u00d7\n  [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo Finance, Aug 2026]. ATAT at a LOWER multiple than\n  HTHT despite higher margins, higher ROE, and similar growth \u2014 but\n  ATAT is smaller. No conclusion from multiples alone; they support\n  the DCF only in direction.\n\nEngine discipline: this is Engine 1, not Engine 4. No optionality\npremium is embedded; the retail business is valued inside the revenue/\nmargin forecast at its actual ~45% revenue mix, not as a \"platform\ncall option.\"\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n1. Competitive response (-2): If ATAT keeps taking upper-midscale\n   share, H World and global majors (Wyndham, IHG) will push into the\n   segment; the 632k-room pipeline [Estimate] confirms supply-side\n   response is ALREADY underway. Expect RevPAR strain.\n2. Reflexivity (+1): High stock price aids franchisee trust and SBC-\n   based talent retention; $150M buybacks show confidence. Conversely,\n   a China-regulatory shock would compress price and trigger passive\n   outflows (79% institutional ownership) \u2014 the negative reflexivity\n   loop is the bear case's accelerant.\n3. Customer behavior (+1): 12M pillows since launch [Actual] suggests\n   the retail brand is moving from early adopters to mainstream.\n   LTV/CAC unverified [Unconfirmed]; watch churn in the retail segment.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN) & EXPECTED PRICE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior (base rates): P(sustained >15% CAGR) \u2248 20-30% [Assumption].\nUpdate via likelihood: Q2 2026 +41% revenue, +29% NI, RevPAR +0.7% vs\nindustry -6%, two guidance raises, 811-hotel pipeline \u2192 posterior\nweight on positive outcomes raised significantly.\n\nSCENARIOS (probabilities sum 100%):\n\u2022 Bear (30%): China consumption shrinks, industry RevPAR -10%+, supply\n  glut; ATAT same-hotel RevPAR falls to ~92% PY, franchisee openings\n  slow to +8%/yr, retail decelerates to +10% with margin pressure.\n  FY30E revenue $2.2B [Assumption], op margin 17.5% [Assumption],\n  FCF 2030 \u2248 $0.26B; IV \u2248 $31/ADS [Estimate].\n  Confidence in this scenario: MEDIUM-HIGH because July industry\n  RevPAR was already -6% [Estimate].\n\u2022 Base (50%): Guidance holds; FY26 +30%, then +22/+16/+12/+9; margins\n  dip then recover. IV = $52/ADS [Estimate] (slight haircut from $53\n  for SBC dilution and share-count verification uncertainty).\n\u2022 Bull (20%): China consumption stabilizes with PBOC easing (China\n  10Y at 1.68% [Actual] is stimulative), ATAT takes disproportionate\n  share in the upper-midscale consolidation; FY30 revenue $3.8B\n  [Assumption], op margin 25.5% [Assumption], IV = $65/ADS [Estimate].\n\nEXPECTED PRICE = 0.30\u00d7$31 + 0.50\u00d7$52 + 0.20\u00d7$65 = $48.3/ADS [Arithmetic]\n50% CI: $44-56 (WACC 9-11%, g 3.0-3.5%, margins \u00b12pp) [Estimate]\n80% CI: $30-67 (scenario range) [Estimate]\nMoS vs base IV: ($52 - $34.75)/$52 = 33% \u2192 STRONG.\nUpside to expected value: +39%.\n\nStep 4-3 Bayesian discipline: if Q2 2026 is the new information and my\nprior was conservative, the posterior is fairly reflected above.\nKILL trigger: any quarter with same-hotel RevPAR <90% PY resets\nposterior toward Bear (this would QUARTER the bull-case probability).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Market implied horizon: at $34.75, fwd P/E 15.7\u00d7 on FY26E EPS $2.22\n  [Estimate] \u2014 the market is effectively pricing ~0-3% EPS growth\n  beyond FY26, i.e., a hard landing.\n\u2022 My horizon: 3-5 years with 17.5% mid-case earnings CAGR (FY26-30).\n\u2022 Spread: >2 years. Arbitrage exists IF the company-specific pipeline\n  (contractual) and brand strength trump the industry cycle. This is\n  the core bet; sized accordingly.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 5-1. Conviction score:\n1. Business quality: 13/15\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 4/5 at $34.75 (MoS 33%)\n3. Macro alignment: 2/5 (headwind)\n4. Thesis clarity (KPIs): 4/5\n5. Execution traceability: 4/5 (audited pack + verified Q2)\nRaw total: 12.5/15.\nAdjustments: Macro headwind -0.5; base-rate red-flag check -0.5.\nFINAL CONVICTION = 11.5/15 \u2192 HIGH. (Conviction decay: -1 per 6\nmonths without confirming evidence.)\n\nStep 5-3. Sizing:\nHigh conviction \u2192 base 5-8%. Macro headwind + China regulatory\ndiscount \u2192 lower half. Crowding -1pp (Section 5.5).\nPRIMARY POSITION TARGET: 5.0% of portfolio; absolute cap 6.0%.\nAdd on dips to $31-32 (near bear-case IV, reduces entry MoS to ~40%);\ntrim at $48-52 (expected value reached).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Short interest: 2.78% of float, 2.53M shares, 2.85 days to cover,\n  +9.5% MoM [Actual \u2014 vendor, Aug 19 2026]. Not crowded; no squeeze\n  fuel; rising shorts are a sentiment headwind.\n\u2022 Institutional ownership: 79.45% [Actual]; passive/ETF-dominated\n  [Assumption] \u2192 forced sellers if any China-index demotion or\n  regulatory action; also means the stock is not held by high-\n  conviction active investors who would know the story.\n\u2022 Insider: 6.15% [Estimate \u2014 vendor]; low for a founder-led Chinese\n  company; possibly multi-class shares not fully captured [Unconfirmed].\n  Governance flag: MODERATE.\n\u2022 Options positioning: not held [Unconfirmed].\n\u2022 Sentiment extreme: price at 35th percentile of 52-wk range\n  ($30.77-$43.17) [Actual]; sell-side mean target $49.46 [Actual \u2014\n  vendor]; consensus is not negative enough to be contrarian-bullish,\n  but the price action is weak. No washout signal yet.\n\u2022 Crowding risk score: 7/15 (high inst ownership, rising shorts,\n  low insider \u2192 moderate). Position-size deduction -1pp (applied).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 ATAT is a China-consumer proxy: positive to RMB stability (+),\n  negative to China macro deterioration. In a broad portfolio, its\n  0.65 vendor beta [Estimate] understates true tail-risk beta to\n  China events (~1.2-1.5 in stress) [Assumption].\n\u2022 Diversification value: high margins, net cash, domestic (RMB)\n   consumption exposure \u2014 uncorrelated with US-tech and US-rates\n   haircuts at the margin.\n\u2022 THE CAP: no China-domiciled single name should exceed 6% of a\n   portfolio with other EM exposure; if the portfolio already has\n   China hotels/consumer names, cap at 4%.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nBinary approximation:\np(success) = 70% (base 50% + bull 20%), average gain = +60%\n(weighted: base $52 = +50%, bull $65 = +87%); q = 30%, avg loss = -11%\n(bear $31).\nFull Kelly f* = (bp - q)/b, b = 0.60 \u2192 f* = (0.60\u00d70.70 - 0.30)/0.60 =\n(0.42 - 0.30)/0.60 = 20% [Arithmetic].\nHalf-Kelly = 10% [Arithmetic]; quarter-Kelly = 5% [Arithmetic].\nLayer 5 target (5%) vs fractional-Kelly (5-10%): gap < 20pp.\n\u2192 Size within Layer-5 bounds. Full Kelly is rejected for single-name\nChina risk.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u