HESIS INTEGRITY)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 7-1. KPI thresholds (quarterly review):\n  KPI                              GREEN          RED (re-evaluate)\n  Same-hotel RevPAR vs PY          \u226595%           <93% for 2 quarters\n  Hotel openings / quarter         \u226580            <50\n  Total revenue growth             \u226520% YoY       <10% YoY\n  Operating margin                 \u226521%           <19%\n  Net cash (RMB)                   \u22653.0B          <2.0B\n  Retail revenue growth            \u226525%           <10%\n  FY27 revenue guidance            \u226515%           withdrawn / <8%\nStep 7-4. PRE-MORTEM (5-year failure):\n1. China consumption collapse \u2192 same-hotel RevPAR -15%, franchisee\n   closures; EARLY WARNING: industry RevPAR -10% for two quarters.\n2. Oversupply + brand dilution \u2192 Atour revPAR premium over industry\n   narrows below 5pp (currently ~6-7pp [Estimate]).\n3. Regulatory/Vie blow-up \u2192 dividend/withholding restrictions, capital\n   control; EARLY WARNING: any PCAOB/CSRC enforcement action, ADS\n   conversion restrictions.\n4. Retail inventory/write-off spiral \u2192 receivables + inventory jump\n   while cash declines; EARLY WARNING: inventory > $60M, or retail\n   op margin < 8%.\n5. Short-reported financial concern \u2192 EARLY WARNING: short interest\n   > 6% of float, or auditor change.\nStep 7-5. Decision journal: T0 $34.75; IV $53 central ($48 EV);\nkey assumptions: FY26-30 CAGR 17.5%, WACC 10%, g 3.5%, tax 28-29%;\nred-team concern: market's China-growth skepticism may be right, and\nthe 30% bear weight may be insufficient.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM (ADVERSARIAL)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. SHORT THESIS (same data):\n1. Industry economics are deteriorating: China hotel RevPAR -6% in\n   July 2026 [Estimate], 632k rooms under construction [Estimate],\n   Hilton guiding -LSD and Marriott +2-3% [Estimate \u2014 Skift]. You are\n   buying a hotel company against the cycle's grain.\n2. ATAT's same-hotel RevPAR is already -3% YoY [Actual]. Blended\n   +0.7% is an artifact of new-hotel mix, not underlying demand.\n3. Retail is ~45% of Q2 revenue [Actual] and LOWER margin; the more\n   it grows, the more net margin falls. Management explicitly guides\n   FY26 margin DOWN [Actual]. The profit engine is being diluted by\n   the revenue engine.\n4. P/B >9\u00d7 [Actual \u2014 vendor], >10\u00d7 per some sources [Estimate \u2014\n   f\u00fatu\u00fan article] on a \"slowing growth\" narrative: multiple\n   compression risk is real.\n5. VIE/regulatory: dividend repatriation and offshore-listing\n   scrutiny [Actual \u2014 20-F risk factors] justify a permanent 20-30%\n   holdco discount \u2014 which implies my $53 is worth only $37-42.\n6. Institutional ownership 79% [Actual]: if any index/ETF flow\n   reverses on China allocation, there is no natural holder.\n7. Short interest rose 9.5% MoM [Actual]; it may know something my\n   model does not (e.g., franchisee attrition data).\n\nStep 9-2. LOGIC COMBAT:\nLong score: 7/10 (execution alpha is real and documented).\nShort score: 6/10 (industry headwinds are real, but the company is\noutperforming and net-cash rich; the \"P/B >10\" argument ignores ROE\n53% and 16% forward P/E).\nGap: 1 \u2192 BORDERLINE. Honest conclusion: this is NOT a high-\nconviction compounder; it is a high-quality growth business in a\ncyclical/regulatory boxing ring. Conviction stays at 11.5, not 13+.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial references: short-seller report (Hindenburg-\nstyle) on ATAT not found [Unconfirmed]. Bear coverage via secondary\nfinancial media [Estimate \u2014 f\u00fatu\u00fan article]. The absence of a\npublished short report lowers the tail-risk of an accounting-specific\nblow-up, but does not eliminate it.\n\nStep 9-4. KILLED ARGUMENTS (with resurrection conditions):\n\u2022 \"China is uninvestable\" \u2014 dismissed; resurrect if capital controls\n   or ADS restrictions actually materialize.\n\u2022 \"Retail will never be profitable\" \u2014 dismissed; resurrect if retail\n   op margin stays <8% beyond FY27.\n\u2022 \"Revenue growth will collapse because industry RevPAR is falling\"\n   \u2014 dismissed because ATAT earnings are fee-driven (not room-revenue\n   driven); resurrect if franchisee openings drop below 50/quarter.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMethodology: Engine 1 selected correctly; alternative engines\n(Engine 4 option-led, Engine 3 hybrid) tested and rejected \u2014 the\nearnings are current, not optionality [Pass].\nValuation: DCF + multiples + scenarios + reverse check (fwd P/E\n15.7\u00d7 at market vs 23.9\u00d7 at IV) [Pass].\nBias: overconfidence check \u2014 base-rate red flag forced the bear case\nto 30%; I did not round the expected value up to the central IV;\nbull case is capped at 20% [Pass].\nConsistency: FY25 share count verified via Q2 EPS cross-check;\nnet debt reconciliation verified (vendor $0.218B = leases $0.182B +\nST debt $0.036B) [Pass].\nNarrative: every forecast driver is tied to a pack citation, a\nretrieved source, or an explicit [Assumption]; no TAM-only language;\nretail P&L is NOT treated as optionality [Pass].\nRed team: completed; conviction adjusted down for gap=1 [Pass].\nData integrity: pack's FY2025 419M share count is UNVERIFIED in the\npack but externally corroborated; segment detail absent; TTM absent;\nquarterly absent; SBC present; all flagged [Pass with caveats].\nFAILURES: none critical. Recalculation triggered by: any revision to\nthe 3:1 ADS ratio [Unconfirmed-resolved], or the FY2025 20-F audit\nreport revealing restatement.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2