 strength: 6.5/10 (RevPAR decline is real, but the fee model is less sensitive; retail dilution is visible but small vs total). Gap = 1.0 < 2.0 \u2192 conviction downgrade from Very High to High (applied in Layer 5). The short case depends on a macro failure; the long case depends on execution of already-contracted units. I side with the long, but with a monitoring regime.\n\n9-3. Adversarial data: I found no Hindenburg-style short-seller report on ATAT in the retrieved sources [Unconfirmed \u2014 none found]. Management's own 20-F disclosures of dividend/transfer restrictions are the most credible adversarial evidence; they are incorporated into the 10% tail and the 8% cap.\n\n9-4. Killed arguments:\n\u2022 \"The vendor beta of 0.65 means low risk\" \u2014 REJECTED: beta window is unknown; a China consumer ADR with a 2-year earnings horizon cannot have 0.65 beta. Killed by fundamental beta 1.0.\n\u2022 \"Net cash $805M fully offsets operating-lease risk\" \u2014 PARTIALLY KILLED: leases are contractual; I exclude them from net debt but acknowledge them as an operating-cost escalator.\n\u2022 \"P/B > 10 means overvalued\" (from Futu article) \u2014 KILLED: ROE 52.9% justifies high P/B; the correct metric is P/E (18.6\u00d7 trailing, 16.3\u00d7 fwd) and EV/EBITDA (8.9\u00d7).\n\u2022 \"Analyst targets are stale\" \u2014 PARTIALLY SURVIVES: mean $49.46 predates the Q2 raise; but my own IV ($50) supports the targets, so this objection does not change the conclusion.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\nA. Methodology: Engine 1 correctly selected; DCF + multiples + reverse DCF + scenarios all used; no single-metric conclusion. PASS.\nB. Valuation: WACC 10.5% derived from current 10Y [Actual] + fundamental beta [Assumption] + ERP [Assumption]; sensitivity range $42\u201366. PASS. Terminal g 3.0% \u2264 nominal GDP. PASS.\nC. Bias: I rejected vendor beta (0.646) as too low and used 1.0 \u2014 conservative. I modeled post-2026 growth decelerating to 9% \u2014 not a hockey stick. No survivorship-bias input; tail scenario retained. PASS.\nD. Consistency: FY2025 figures are [Filed] at FY25-avg FX ~7.08; forward build is in RMB at 6.80 \u2014 the FX vintage is explicit and the net-cash bridge is converted at the same 6.80. No time-point mixing: T-1 = FY2025 (10-K), Tpf = Q2 2026 (8-K/PR), T0 = 2026-08-24. PASS.\nE. Narrative: Retail \"platform\" claim is supported by numbers (120M members, +67% retail growth [Estimate]) but I did NOT add a separate platform premium \u2014 the DCF captures it only through revenue/margin. PASS.\nF. Red team: Section 9 produced a seven-point short thesis; logic gap 1.0 applied; conviction 14\u219212.5. PASS.\nG. Data integrity: Resolution of ADS-vs-ordinary shares (3:1) removed a 3\u00d7 distortion. The pack's \"not available\" fields were not treated as zero. Debt-overlap uncertainty was disclosed and only one count of short-term debt ($36M) was used. Segment data was unavailable [Unconfirmed] \u2014 the DCF build uses consolidated margins, which is the honest fallback. PASS with declared gaps.\nH. Linearity check: If WACC = 9% \u2192 IV $66; if 12% \u2192 $42. If margin = 21.5% \u2192 $46. The buy case survives stress; the position is sized for the tail. PASS.\n\nAudit outcome: PASS (37/37 checks, with the disclosure caveats above).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550