t] \u2014 FY2025 showed a +$124M cash source; modeling 0 is conservative (no repeat tailwind). [Assumption]\n\nStep 3-2. Discount Rate (WACC) Derivation:\n- Risk-free: 4.70% US 10Y (FRED, 2026-08-21) [Actual]\n- Equity risk premium: 6.0% (China ADR premium incl. governance/VoIP risk) [Assumption]\n- Beta: 1.0 (pack provider beta 0.646 is unverified and likely understates China ADR macro risk) [Assumption]\n- Cost of equity: 4.7% + 1.0 \u00d7 6.0% = 10.7%\n- Debt: none \u2014 WACC \u2248 CoE, with zero-debt balance sheet.\n- Adopted WACC: 10.5% [Assumption] (slight benefit for net-cash and low beta, rounded)\n- Sensitivity: IV at 9.5% = $53; at 11.5% = $41.\n\nStep 3-3. Terminal Value:\n- Terminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption] \u2014 below long-term China nominal GDP; platform in mature market.\n- Terminal FCF = 0.517 \u00d7 1.03 = 0.533; TV = 0.533/(0.105\u22120.03) = $7.10B\n\nStep 3-4. DCF Value:\n- PV of 2026\u20132030 FCF (mid-year convention, 10.5%): $1.54B [Arithmetic]\n- PV of TV: $4.31B [Arithmetic]\n- EV = $5.85B\n- Add net cash: $0.623B [Estimate] (components for net debt: cash $475M + ST investments $366M \u2212 ST borrowings/current portion $36M \u2212 operating leases $182M; overlap between 6B columns may make this imprecise)\n- Equity value: $6.47B\n- Per ADS (137.46M): $47.0 [Estimate]\n\nStep 3-5. Multiples Cross-Check:\n- P/E on FY2026E EPS: my model NI \u2248 $0.28B \u2192 EPS $2.04 \u2192 23.0x at IV $47; at T0 $34.75: forward P/E \u2248 17.0x (consensus EPS RMB 15.24 = $2.18: 15.9x) [Estimate]\n- PEG (growth 20%+): ~0.8\u20131.0 \u2014 reasonable for a high-ROE compounder\n- EV/EBITDA: IV EV $5.85B / 2026E EBITDA (OI 0.40 + D&A 0.018 + SBC 0.02) \u2248 $0.44B = 13.3x [Estimate]\n- P/B 9.1x [Actual] on ROE 53% \u2014 justified by franchise economics; not a standalone metric\n- Peer comparison: [Unconfirmed \u2014 research budget exhausted; China hotel ADR peers (HTHT, GreenTree, Jinjiang) trade roughly 12\u201320x forward but not verified.]\n\nStep 3-6. Reverse DCF (T0 price):\n- EV at T0 = $4.777B - $0.623B = $4.154B\n- 2026E FCF $0.291B \u2192 14.3x. With 16\u201317% FCF margin and 16.8% revenue CAGR, the market is implying ~5-year FCF CAGR of ~10\u201312% (then 3% terminal) [Estimate]. \n- Verdict: Market prices a materially slower growth path than the base case. This is the core source of upside if execution continues.\n\n3-X. Tornado Sensitivity \u2014 Top 3 variables (these are the Thesis KPIs):\n1. Revenue CAGR 2026\u20132030 (range 10\u201320% vs base 16.8%): IV 37\u201358\n2. WACC (9.5%\u201311.5%): IV 53\u201341\n3. 2030 operating margin (22%\u201326%): IV 44\u201351\n\nBase IV: $47.0 \u2192 Expected (probability-weighted): $46 (see Section 4).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive Response: Pipeline of upper-midscale hotels in China hit record 1,287 projects (Daily Lodging Report, 2026-08-06) [Estimate \u2014 secondary]. Competitors (Huazhu, Jinjiang, GreenTree, IHG) will add supply, pressuring ADR/occupancy. 2026 RevPAR is already flat (+0.6% YoY in Q2). Competitive-response score: -2 (headwind).\n\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity: Positive \u2014 2,175 hotels + rising ADR attracts franchisees (pipeline 811) and retail customers; brand feeds on itself. Negative: if RevPAR declines 2\u20133 quarters, franchisee economics sour, pipeline shrinks, retail halo fades. Balanced: +1.\n\nStep 3.5-3. Customer Behavior: Business travelers are the core hotel base (stable, but corporate budgets tighten in China's slow recovery); retail is in the \"early-early mainstream\" phase (63% growth). LTV/CAC: not disclosed [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN-UPDATED)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 4-1. Scenario set (probabilities sum to 100%):\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Description | Terminal revenue CAGR 2026\u201330 | OP margin 2030 | IV ($/ADS) |\n|----------|------------|-------------|-------------------------------|----------------|------------|\n| Bear | 25% | China consumption pause; RevPAR -5%/yr; hotel openings slow; retail growth halves; guidance repeatedly missed; dilution continues | 8% | 20% | ~$30 |\n| Base | 50% | Continuation of scaled franchise growth + retail moderation to 20\u201325%; RevPAR ~flat; margins recover by 2030 | 16.8% | 24% | ~$47 |\n| Bull | 25% | Service consumption upgrade accelerates; retail sustains 30%+; hotel network expands to 4,000+; margin expansion beats | 22% | 26% | ~$59 |\n\nStep 4-2. Probability assignment logic:\n- Base 50% (modal): 